  <section|Inputs and notation><label|inputs-and-notation>

  The prose uses ordinary polynomial and Euclidean-moment language. Its
  inputs are the pinned source's finite polynomial jet spaces, the
  gauge-invariant weighted grading, the free Wick moments on separated
  configurations, reflection positivity, the compact simple gauge group's
  color pairing, and the spin/reality/covariance subspace of the finite-level
  vector charge. The fixed capacity is chosen once from the bounded-jet
  invariant ideal generators, the host-product bound, and the largest
  mixed-circulation test. It is independent of shell, polynomial length, and
  the finite field level.

  Internal Ward-map erasure is intentionally not proved in this unit. The
  parent-owned <verbatim|manuscript/existence/free-internal-ward-erasure.tex>,
  label <verbatim|sec:free-internal-ward-erasure>, is the separate unit for
  that input. The selected-scale application in
  <verbatim|physical-ward-propagation.tex> also requires its stated
  same-family observer/row convergence; this unit does not prove those
  interacting-theory inputs.

