  <verbatim|sec:free-internal-ward-erasure>>>>>>

  <section|Literature and editorial decisions><label|literature-and-editorial-decisions>

  The finite-generation step uses the Hilbert basis theorem for polynomial
  rings in finitely many variables: the ideal is generated by the family of
  positive-length invariant homogeneous polynomials, and finite generators
  can be selected from that family. Compact-group averaging is normalized
  Haar integration and is used only to make the coefficient factors
  invariant. No YM-specific external theorem is invoked. The Wick collision
  and reflection-positivity steps are proved in the manuscript using the free
  moments' stated properties. The exact source flow is grouped into three
  mathematical arguments rather than translated one helper at a time.

  The external detector's source induction sets <verbatim|j=dim Lie(G)>,
  chooses a host bound <verbatim|r_j>, and uses capacity at least
  <verbatim|max(r_j, 4+j+(j+1))>; the latter covers the extra probe of order
  <verbatim|j+1> with every order <verbatim|\<less\>j> probe. The
  quiet-charge proof follows the source sequence: opposite-reflection degree
  reduction, panel representation, the triangular three-point collision, the
  two parity projections and cross-seed, then the localized flux commutator
  and weighted-degree/opposite-reflection parity. Its dilation identity is
  supplied by the parent-owned radial-flux unit, not inferred from
  translation or rotation Ward identities. The finite-scene proof is the
  source's strict-order perturbation plus analytic continuation along a
  collision-free segment and finite-dimensional kernel selection.

  <section|Open obligations and evidence><label|open-obligations-and-evidence>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>The quiet-charge theorem is stated on the finite
    spin-covariant/reality/unit subspace, with the filtration condition at
    each grade through the cutoff. Independent mathematics/source review
    remains pending for the panel, collision, and finite sign-classification
    arguments.

    <item>The mixed-collision input is the reviewed parent theorem
    <verbatim|thm:free-circulation-null>; the application states its jet
    cutoff, capacity, and strict lower/upper probe order hypotheses. The
    fixed-shelf finite-generation and top-shelf elimination arguments remain
    local proof obligations for review.

    <item>The selected interacting family still needs same-run finite-row
    convergence and free-data alignment; those are not proved here.

    <item>Internal-map erasure is delegated to the separate parent-owned unit
    above.

    <item>Commands run: targeted <verbatim|rg>/<verbatim|sed> inspection of
    declarations and immediate dependencies; <verbatim|python3
    scripts/check_blueprint.py> failed because this clone has no
    <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json>. No Lean build or LaTeX
    build was run.

    <item>Status remains draft until independent mathematics and
    source-correspondence reviews pass.
  </itemize-minus>

